---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { useTranslations } from '../../i18n/utils';
import { Info, CircleQuestionMark, BookOpen, MessagesSquare, PenLine } from '@lucide/astro';

const lang = 'en' as const;
const t = useTranslations(lang);

const faqItems = [
  {
    question: 'Is a will required by law?',
    answer:
      "No, a will is not required. Without one, the law decides who inherits, and that isn't always what you would choose.",
  },
  {
    question: 'What is the difference between a will and a living will?',
    answer:
      'A will arranges what happens to your belongings after you pass away. A living will arranges who decides for you if you no longer can, for example due to illness.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I change my will later?',
    answer:
      'You can have your will updated by a notary, for example after moving, a divorce, or the birth of a child.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is an executor?',
    answer:
      'An executor is the person who settles your estate after you pass away: closing accounts, paying debts, and distributing belongings. You appoint this person yourself in your will.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is a bequest?',
    answer:
      'A bequest is a fixed amount, item, or right that you leave to a specific person or charity, separate from the rest of your estate.',
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Why do you need a will?"
  description="Without a will, the law decides who inherits. Read what you can arrange in a will and how the process works."
  pageKey="testament"
  datePublished="2026-09-19"
  dateModified="2026-09-20"
  faqItems={faqItems}
>
  <article>
    <h1>Why do you need a will?</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      Without a will, the law decides who inherits. That isn't always what
      you want. With a will, you decide this yourself, and you protect your
      partner and children.
    </p>

    <div class="disclaimer-box">
      <Info size={20} stroke-width={1.75} />
      <p>{t('disclaimer.short')}</p>
    </div>

    <h2>What happens if you don't have a will?</h2>
    <p>
      Without a will, statutory inheritance law applies. The law then names
      your heirs: the people who are legally entitled to inherit. First in
      line are your partner and children. After them come parents, and
      brothers and sisters.
    </p>
    <p>
      Do you live together unmarried, without a cohabitation agreement and
      without a will? Then your partner inherits nothing in that case. The
      same applies to stepchildren: they never inherit automatically.
    </p>

    <h2>What can you arrange in a will?</h2>
    <p>
      A will is more than deciding who inherits. You can include several
      elements, each with its own purpose.
    </p>

    <h3>Naming your heirs</h3>
    <p>
      You decide who inherits, and for what share. This can be your partner,
      your children, a charity, or someone else who is dear to you.
    </p>

    <h3>Arranging guardianship</h3>
    <p>
      Do you have minor children? Then you set out who takes care of them if
      you and the other parent are no longer there. Without this
      arrangement, a judge decides who becomes guardian.
    </p>

    <h3>Appointing an executor</h3>
    <p>
      An executor handles the practical matters after you pass away: closing
      accounts, paying debts, and dividing belongings among the heirs.
      Without an executor, the heirs handle this together themselves.
    </p>

    <h3>Leaving a bequest</h3>
    <p>
      With a bequest, you leave a fixed amount, an item, or for example a
      piece of jewelry to a specific person or charity, separate from the
      rest of your estate.
    </p>

    <h2>Will or cohabitation agreement: what covers what?</h2>
    <p>
      A cohabitation agreement mainly arranges matters between you and your
      partner during your life, such as sharing costs and property. A will
      arranges what happens after you pass away. If you live together
      unmarried, you often need both to properly protect your partner.
    </p>

    <h2>What does this mean for a blended family?</h2>
    <p class="example-box">
      Say you have a new partner, and together you also have children from
      earlier relationships. Without a will, only your own children
      automatically inherit from you. Your partner and stepchildren then
      receive nothing, unless you set this out in a will.
    </p>

    <h2>How do you write a will?</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <BookOpen class="step-icon" size={20} stroke-width={1.75} aria-hidden="true" />
        <strong>Think about your wishes.</strong> Who should inherit, who
        becomes guardian, and do you have any special wishes?
      </li>
      <li>
        <MessagesSquare class="step-icon" size={20} stroke-width={1.75} aria-hidden="true" />
        <strong>Make an appointment with a notary.</strong> The notary
        explains your options in a personal conversation.
      </li>
      <li>
        <PenLine class="step-icon" size={20} stroke-width={1.75} aria-hidden="true" />
        <strong>Discuss and sign the draft.</strong> Adjust the will where
        needed, and sign the deed at the notary's office.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2><CircleQuestionMark class="heading-icon" size={22} stroke-width={1.75} aria-hidden="true" />{t('faq.heading')}</h2>
    <dl>
      {faqItems.map((item) => (
        <div class="faq-item">
          <dt>{item.question}</dt>
          <dd>{item.answer}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <h2>{t('sources.heading')}</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.rijksoverheid.nl">Rijksoverheid</a> (Dutch government) &mdash; information on inheritance law</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.knb.nl">KNB</a> (Royal Dutch Association of Civil-law Notaries) &mdash; helps you find a notary</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.belastingdienst.nl">Belastingdienst</a> (Dutch Tax Administration) &mdash; information on inheritance tax</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="meta-line">These sources were consulted in 2026.</p>

    <p class="meta-line">{t('lastchecked.label')}: 20 September 2026</p>

    <p class="cta-row">
      <a class="button" href="/wachtlijst">Join the waitlist (Dutch)</a>
      <a class="button-secondary" href="/en/">{t('cta.back_home')}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
